<section class="hero">
  <h1>Compile LaTeX through an HTTP API</h1>
  <p class="page-lead">
    LaTeX-on-HTTP takes your LaTeX sources — inline content, files or remote
    URLs — and returns the compiled PDF. No local TeX installation required:
    call it from server code, CI pipelines or the browser.
  </p>
  <div class="hero-actions">
    <a class="button button-primary" href="{{ rootPrefix }}playground/index.html">Try the live playground →</a>
    <a class="button button-secondary" href="{{ rootPrefix }}api/builds-sync/index.html">API reference</a>
  </div>
</section>

